# Tagged enum variant casing

In `frontend/src` and `api/src`, every `Data.TaggedEnum`/`Data.taggedEnum` variant tag must be
PascalCase, not camelCase. This matches the `_tag` convention used elsewhere in `effect`
(`Schema.TaggedError`, `Option.Some`/`Option.None`, `Either.Left`/`Either.Right`).

The constructors destructured from `Data.taggedEnum(...)` keep the same PascalCase names, and
`$match`'s handler keys follow the tag names exactly.

```ts
// BAD: camelCase variant tags
type HealthState = Data.TaggedEnum<{
  readonly fetching: {};
  readonly ok: {};
  readonly error: {};
}>;
const { fetching, ok, error, $match } = Data.taggedEnum<HealthState>();

// GOOD: PascalCase variant tags
type HealthState = Data.TaggedEnum<{
  readonly Fetching: {};
  readonly Ok: {};
  readonly Error: {};
}>;
const { Fetching, Ok, Error, $match } = Data.taggedEnum<HealthState>();

$match(state, {
  Fetching: () => ...,
  Ok: () => ...,
  Error: () => ...,
});
```
